%[text] # Getting started with scalebar
%[text] `scalebar` adds horizontal and vertical scale bars to MATLAB axes. This guide introduces the modern name-value API and points to the complete runnable examples.
%%
%[text] ## Setup
%[text] Run this saved file from the MATLAB Live Editor. The editor provides the document's real path so the source and examples can be located from a repository checkout.
activeDocument = matlab.desktop.editor.getActiveFilename;
if isempty(activeDocument) || startsWith(activeDocument, "Untitled")
    error("scalebar:GettingStartedRequiresSavedLiveScript", ...
        "Save GettingStarted.m and run it from the MATLAB Live Editor.")
end

sourceRoot = fileparts(activeDocument);
addpath(fullfile(sourceRoot, "scalebar"), fullfile(sourceRoot, "examples"))
%%
%[text] ## Quick start
%[text] Create an image and add a horizontal scale bar. The default `Axis="x"` creates a horizontal bar.
hAxes = axes(); %[output:4297707a]
imagesc(hAxes, peaks(256)) %[output:4297707a]
axis(hAxes, "image", "off") %[output:4297707a]
colormap(hAxes, turbo) %[output:4297707a]

hScalebar = scalebar(hAxes, 50, "pixels", ... %[output:group:51e839ac] %[output:4297707a]
    Location="southeast", Color="w", LineWidth=2); %[output:group:51e839ac] %[output:4297707a]
%%
%[text] ## Calibrated image
%[text] The complete image example uses MATLAB's `cell.tif` sample image and requires Image Processing Toolbox. It adds a 25 $\\mu$m scale bar using the image calibration.
createImageExample(); %[output:7db439f4]
%%
%[text] ## Plot data
%[text] The plot example creates a simulated membrane-potential trace. It uses `Axis="x"` for a 500 ms time bar and `Axis="y"` for a 50 mV magnitude bar.
createPlotExample(); %[output:789cccdd]
%%
%[text] ## Next steps
%[text] Use the returned `hScalebar` object to adjust properties such as `Location`, `Color`, and `TextSpacing`. See the README for all supported name-value options.

